#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105516 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ba6b6b5-ac1d-5a3a-876a-af51fdf50e0a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Scalar Triple Product Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "2f380683-0d93-541d-a07d-95a1d889c761" :question/math-academy-id "e-4347" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-3,2 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -1,0,5 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1,2,3 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ - 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( 0 \\cdot  3 - 5 \\cdot  2 ) \\mathbf{i} - ( - 1 \\cdot  3 - 5 \\cdot  1 ) \\mathbf{j} + ( - 1 \\cdot  2 - 0 \\cdot  2 ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - 10 \\mathbf{i} + 8 \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 10 , 8 , - 2 \\rangle\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\langle  2 , - 3 , 2 \\rangle  \\cdot  \\langle  - 10 , 8 , - 2 \\rangle \\\\  & = 2 \\cdot  ( - 10 ) + ( - 3 ) \\cdot  8 + 2 \\cdot  ( - 2 ) \\\\  & = - 48\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105517 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Scalar Triple Product Using a Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "b5cf98f2-087d-580c-a2f6-c37ad2af4c2c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4348" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,2,-1 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,2,1 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,-1,2 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a}$, $\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}4 & 2 & - 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = 4 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert - 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 2 \\\\ - 1 & - 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = 4 \\cdot  ( 2 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) - 2 \\cdot  ( 0 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  ( 0 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) - 2 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) \\\\  & = 20 - 2 - 2 \\\\  & = 16.\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Scalar Triple Products Using Its Properties"}] :question/id #uuid "483b758a-9b14-5a72-87e5-70f27a0acf48" :question/math-academy-id "e-4349" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$, if $2\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times 3\\mathbf{c}) = 5$." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}2 \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  3 \\mathbf{c} ) & = 5 \\\\ 2 \\cdot  [ \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  3 \\mathbf{c} ) ] & = 5 \\\\ 2 \\cdot  3 \\cdot  [ \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) ] & = 5 \\\\ \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\frac{5}{6} .\\end{array}$$\n\nThen, we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ to get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{c} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{a} ) & = - \\frac{5}{6} ,\\end{array}$$\n\nand again we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ to get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{c} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} ) & = \\frac{5}{6} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Scalar Triple Products Using Its Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5b2509-1ebc-5cb8-9760-cf26fbfd0a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102562} {:answer/id #uuid "f689ea4c-19f9-5856-b486-0363e108d13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102563} {:answer/id #uuid "3036e373-f469-5fe1-9d96-32e33aec3f85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102564} {:answer/id #uuid "35450a06-9752-5f0c-ab91-c41005999b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 1, 0, 3\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102565} {:answer/id #uuid "67c76fac-9f06-5c2e-9d19-f1f2f39feef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3036e373-f469-5fe1-9d96-32e33aec3f85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebce03e2-8b30-5b5a-9fdc-f5862466128f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102561}] :question/id #uuid "0db80f94-e2a5-583e-875d-ce7dd7157cf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20062" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{a} )$, if $\\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} = \\langle  2 , 3 , 0 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{a} = \\langle  1 , - 2 , 2 \\rangle  .$."}]}
